# Web tests

Unit tests run on Karma and Jasmine (`pnpm test`). Cover ViewModels and use cases with no DOM and no HTTP. Catalog keys used by a screen (starting with `es-CO`) need a Karma spec. Do not switch the runner to Vitest.

E2E scenarios are Gherkin (`Given` / `When` / `Then`) executed by Cucumber and Playwright against the nginx URL (`BASE_URL`).

- Page objects own every locator. Steps call page objects only.
- Locate elements with `data-testid` via `getByTestId`. No `xpath` or `css` in steps or page objects.
- Wait on Playwright auto-waits or `waitFor`. No `sleep()`.

```ts
// ❌ BAD
await page.locator('h1').click();
await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, 1000));

// ✅ GOOD
await this.page.getByTestId('nav-cms').click();
await this.page.getByTestId('cms-shell').waitFor({ state: 'visible' });
```
